+Subdomain Matching
+==================
+
+To match rules against a subdomain, pass ``subdomain_matching=True`` to the
+:class:`Map` constructor and give the `subdomain` argument to the relevant
+rules. When binding with :meth:`Map.bind_to_environ`, the current subdomain is
+then detected by removing the configured ``server_name`` from the request's
+host::
+
+    url_map = Map([
+        Rule('/', endpoint='www_index', subdomain='www'),
+        Rule('/', endpoint='help_index', subdomain='help')
+    ], subdomain_matching=True)
+
+If it is not enabled, ``bind_to_environ`` ignores the host when determining the
+subdomain, so passing ``server_name`` does not restrict which hosts can be
+routed.
+
+.. versionadded:: 3.2
+    The ``subdomain_matching`` parameter.
+
+
 Host Matching
 =============
 
